  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>INSEEC Business School is a French private business school. Founded in 1975, INSEEC is a member of France’s Conférence des Grandes Écoles (CGE), positioning it among the country’s most respected institutions of higher learning. Its acronym INSEEC stands for Institut des Hautes Études Economiques et Commerciales (Institute of Higher Studies in Economics and Commerce).</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At INSEEC Business School, your student life will be vibrant with many clubs, events, and support services to help you all the time. The school organises numerous events throughout the year, including conferences, career fairs, and skill-building workshops to expand your professional network. You’ll also have access to mental health resources and activities.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>INSEEC does not provide on-campus housing, but it offers support to help you find suitable accommodation nearby. The school works closely with local housing providers to offer a range of options to meet your needs. These include private apartments, shared flats, and student residences near the campuses.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
